Chiming in as a new Bevy user. This bit me in the butt today.

Here's a minimal example if that's at all helpful:

```rust
use bevy::prelude::*;

fn main() {
    App::new()
        .add_plugins(DefaultPlugins)
        .add_state(AppState::A)
        .add_system(log_state_change)
        .run();
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Eq, PartialEq, Hash)]
enum AppState {
    A,
    B,
}

fn log_state_change(app_state: Res<State<AppState>>) {
    if app_state.is_changed() {
        info!("App state changed: {:?}", app_state.current());
    }
}
```

This produces log spam on every frame, when the expected behavior would be no log spam.

On a related note, I found myself wanting a `previous()` method on the `State` struct, in addition to `current()`.

